  "name": "VON WILLEBRAND FACTOR RISTOCETIN COFACTOR ASSAY(vWF:RCO)",
  "code": "1633",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>Note :<br>1. Von Willebrand factor ristocetin cofactor activity (VWF:Rco) test result may be affected by presence of hemoglobin &gt;500 mg/dL, bilirubin &gt; 18 mg/dL, triglycerides &gt;1250 mg/dL, human anti-mouse antibody (HAMA) &gt;1&micro;g/Ml and Rheumatoid factor &gt;800IU/mL.<br>2. Individuals of Blood Group &ldquo;O&rdquo; may have lower vWF:RCo activity than those of other ABO blood groups.<br>3. Test conducted on citrated plasma.</p>\n<p>Comments<br>Von Willebrand factor ristocetin cofactor activity (VWF:Rco) assay determines the activity of von Willebrand factor plasma protein and is used for the basic screening of von Willebrand disease. Von Willebrand factor plays a key role in Primary &amp; Secondary hemostasis. In the latter role it serves as a carrier protein for Factor VIII. It is the most common inherited bleeding disorder characterized by easy bruising and prolonged bleeding from mucosal surfaces.</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9508%;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 18.1606%;\"><col style=\"width: 81.784%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>TYPE</td>\n<td>REMARKS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Partial quantitative deficiency of vWF</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Qualitative deficiency of vWF</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2A</td>\n<td>Decreased platelet dependent vWF function with selective deficiency of High molecular weight multimers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2B</td>\n<td>Increased affinity for platelet glycoprotein 1b</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2M</td>\n<td>Decreased platelet dependent vWF function with normal High molecular weight multimers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2N</td>\n<td>Markedly decreased binding of Factor VIII to vWF</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Complete deficiency of vWF</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
